await t("Team board handoffs: Designer→Coder, Coder→Tester, Tester→Reviewer (log + events)", () => { const h = HAPPY.board.handoffs.map((x) => `${x.from}>${x.to}`); const ev = HAPPY.ev.filter((e) => e.type === "handoff").length; return must(h.join() === "Designer>Coder,Coder>Tester,Tester>Reviewer" && ev === 3 && HAPPY.board.log.some((l) => /Designer → Coder/.test(l.text)), h.join()); });
await t("Team board (team.json): 4 roles ke tasks + brain likha + budget", () => { const roles = new Set(HAPPY.board.tasks.map((x) => x.role)); return must(["designer", "coder", "tester", "reviewer"].every((r) => roles.has(r)) && HAPPY.board.roles.designer.brain === "mock-designer" && HAPPY.board.roles.tester.brain.includes("bina AI") && HAPPY.board.budget.calls === 3 && HAPPY.board.budget.used > 0); });
await t("Team: board ki todo list UI ko (Team board pane)", () => { const td = HAPPY.ev.filter((e) => e.type === "todo").at(-1); return must(td && td.items.length === 4 && td.items.every((x) => x.startsWith("[x]"))); });
await t("Team: memory prompts mein (Designer system mein MEMORY)", async () => { const m = mockTeam({ coder: () => W("index.html", GOOD_HTML) + "\n" + W("style.css", CSS) }); await runT(m); const sys = m.calls.find((c) => c.role === "designer").messages[0].content; return must(/MEMORY/.test(sys) && /Roman Urdu/.test(sys)); });
await t("Team finish: project khulasa memory mein + .faheem-agent.json (Jaari rakho)", () => { const p = MEM.listMemories({ type: "project" }); const hist = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(HAPPY.dir, ".faheem-agent.json"), "utf8")); return must(p.length >= 1 && /\[Team\]/.test(hist.at(-1).summary)); });
await t("Team: Tester fail → Coder fix → pass (seekh memory mein)", async () => { const before = MEM.listMemories({ type: "lesson" }).length; const m = mockTeam({ coder: (n) => (n === 1 ? W("index.html", GOOD_HTML) : W("style.css", CSS)) }); const r = await runT(m); const h = r.board.handoffs.map((x) => `${x.from}>${x.to}`); const after = MEM.listMemories({ type: "lesson" }); return must(h.includes("Tester>Coder") && r.board.status === "done" && after.length === before + 1 && /style\.css/.test(after[0].text), h.join()); });
await t("Team: Browser test ghalti bhi Coder ko wapas (mock runtimeTest)", async () => { let n = 0; const m = mockTeam({ coder: () => W("index.html", GOOD_HTML) + "\n" + W("style.css", CSS) }); const r = await runT(m, { runtimeTest: async () => (++n === 1 ? { ok: false, errors: ["TypeError: x is null"] } : { ok: true }) }); return must(r.board.handoffs.some((x) => x.from === "Tester" && x.to === "Coder" && /browser test/.test(x.note)) && r.board.status === "done"); });
await t("Team: Reviewer issues → Coder round 2", async () => { let rv = 0; const m = mockTeam({ coder: () => W("index.html", GOOD_HTML) + "\n" + W("style.css", CSS), reviewer: () => (++rv === 1 ? '{"ok":false,"issues":["Contact page missing"],"summary":"x"}' : '{"ok":true,"summary":"theek"}') }); const r = await runT(m); return must(r.board.handoffs.some((x) => x.from === "Reviewer" && x.to === "Coder") && m.calls.filter((c) => c.role === "coder").length === 2 && /Contact page missing/.test(m.calls.filter((c) => c.role === "coder")[1].messages[1].content)); });
await t("Team: Reviewer brain na mile to bhi done (tests pass the)", async () => { const m = mockTeam({ coder: () => W("index.html", GOOD_HTML) + "\n" + W("style.css", CSS), reviewer: () => { const e = new Error("all limit"); e.code = "BRAINS"; throw e; } }); const r = await runT(m); const d = r.ev.find((e) => e.type === "done"); return must(d && !d.partial && r.board.status === "done"); });
await t("Fallback: Designer ke brains limit → single Agent Mode", async () => { let fb = 0; const m = mockTeam({ designer: () => { throw new TM.BrainsError("sab brains limit"); }, coder: () => "" }); const r = await runT(m, { fallback: async () => { fb++; } }); return must(fb === 1 && r.board.status === "fallback" && r.ev.some((e) => /Single Agent Mode/.test(e.text || ""))); });
await t("Fallback: Coder ne koi file nahi likhi → single Agent Mode", async () => { let fb = 0; const m = mockTeam({ coder: () => "Sorry, main nahi kar sakta." }); const r = await runT(m, { fallback: async () => { fb++; } }); return must(fb === 1 && r.board.status === "fallback"); });
await t("Fallback: Coder brains limit (files pehle se) → partial, files mehfooz", async () => { const m = mockTeam({ coder: (n) => { if (n === 1) return W("index.html", GOOD_HTML); throw new TM.BrainsError("limit"); } }); let fb = 0; const r = await runT(m, { fallback: async () => { fb++; } }); const d = r.ev.find((e) => e.type === "done"); return must(fb === 0 && d?.partial && fs.existsSync(path.join(r.dir, "index.html"))); });
await t("Budget guard: maxCalls=2 → team rukti hai (2 se zyada call nahi)", async () => { const m = mockTeam({ coder: (n) => (n === 1 ? W("index.html", GOOD_HTML) : W("style.css", CSS)) }); const r = await runT(m, { options: { maxCalls: 2 } }); const d = r.ev.find((e) => e.type === "done"); return must(m.calls.length === 2 && d?.partial && /had/i.test(d.summary) && r.board.status === "partial", `${m.calls.length} ${d?.summary}`); });
await t("Budget guard: token budget chhota → koi brain call nahi", async () => { const m = mockTeam({ coder: () => "" }); const r = await runT(m, { options: { maxTokens: 50 } }); const d = r.ev.find((e) => e.type === "done"); return must(m.calls.length === 0 && d?.partial && /budget/i.test(d.summary)); });
await t("Max rounds: Tester hamesha fail → 3 rounds ke baad ruk (partial)", async () => { const m = mockTeam({ coder: () => W("index.html", "<html><body><button onclick=\"nahiHai()\">x</button></body></html>") }); const r = await runT(m); const d = r.ev.find((e) => e.type === "done"); return must(m.calls.filter((c) => c.role === "coder").length === 3 && d?.partial && /Rounds khatam/.test(d.summary)); });
await t("Team: Roko (abort) se ruk jati hai", async () => { const ac = new AbortController(); const m = mockTeam({ designer: () => { ac.abort(); return "FILES: index.html"; }, coder: () => W("index.html", GOOD_HTML) }); const r = await runT(m, { signal: ac.signal }); return must(!m.calls.some((c) => c.role === "coder") && !r.ev.some((e) => e.type === "done" && !e.partial)); });
await t("Team: files sirf project folder ke andar (../ rad)", async () => { const m = mockTeam({ designer: () => "FILES: index.html", coder: () => W("../evil.html", "<html></html>") + "\n" + W("index.html", GOOD_HTML.replace('<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">', "")) }); const r = await runT(m); return must(!fs.existsSync(path.join(path.dirname(r.dir), "evil.html")) && fs.existsSync(path.join(r.dir, "index.html"))); });
await t("API: team sirf body.team === true par; Team mode default band", () => must(/if \(body\.team === true\) await runTeamMode/.test(rd("app/api/agent/route.js")) && /teamMode: false/.test(rd("lib/prefs.js"))));
await t("UI: Agent Mode 'Team' toggle + handoff log, Options mein Team + Memory cards", () => { const a = rd("app/agent/page.js"), o = rd("app/options/page.js"); return must(/data-team-toggle/.test(a) && /e\.type === "handoff"/.test(a) && /team, images/.test(a) && /data-team-option/.test(o) && /data-memory-option/.test(o) && /href="\/memory"/.test(o)); });
